{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QFkiRJDeC3bJeZ3hKaEwvG","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"brace_checklist\": \"2026-10-01\",\n  \"repo\": \"\",\n  \"commit\": null,\n  \"reviewed_at\": \"2026-10-02T18:00:52Z\",\n  \"scope\": \"TODO: what was reviewed and what wasn't.\",\n  \"review_protocol\": \"coverage-first-v1\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"item\": \"R09\",\n      \"gate\": \"G3\",\n      \"title\": \"Sequence and context-aware detection\",\n      \"requirement\": \"Test suspicious chains of actions that are each allowed on their own. Also test unusual fan-out and resource use. Compare behavior across context-size ranges, so one fleet-wide baseline doesn't hide failures in long contexts. If the agent could be hijacked while using only allowed tools, check each high-impact action against the original task before it runs. Use a checker that doesn't see the untrusted content in between, and measure what it misses.\",\n      \"not_covered\": [\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Encoded payloads or writes outside scope going undetected\",\n          \"owner\": \"R08\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"No test against a deliberately evasive, misaligned agent\",\n          \"owner\": \"R10\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Context size not logged for each action decision\",\n          \"owner\": \"R07\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"rating\": \"needs_evidence\",\n      \"confidence\": \"low\",\n      \"evidence\": [],\n      \"checks\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"R09.1\",\n          \"check\": \"Detection rules evaluate sequences of calls across a run (for example many reads followed by an outside send), not only single calls.\",\n448:- Behavior not compared across context-size ranges → **R09**\n506:- Chains of individually allowed actions going undetected → **R09**\n507:- No test of a second-model review against evasive behavior → **R10**\n535:## R09 · G3 · C7/Obs-T2 — Sequence and context-aware detection\n559:- **R09.1** Detection rules evaluate sequences of calls across a run (for example many reads followed by an outside send), not only single calls.\n561:- **R09.2** Rules cover unusual fan-out and resource use.\n563:- **R09.3** Thresholds or baselines are set per context-size range, not as one fleet-wide value.\n565:- **R09.4** If hijack through allowed tools alone is possible, each high-impact action is checked against the original task before it runs, by a checker that is not given the untrusted content.\n573:- No test against a deliberately evasive, misaligned agent → **R10**\n596:**Needs runtime evidence:** Catch and false-alarm rates per context-size range against thresholds set before the run. Recipe R09.\n600:## R10 · G3 · C7 — Misaligned-behavior review\n632:- Chains of individually allowed actions going undetected → **R09**\n653:**Needs runtime evidence:** Measured misses and false alarms on a labeled evasive set, plus red-team runs. Code can only show a reviewer exists. Recipe R10.\n657:## R11 · G1 · C8 — Tested kill switch\n675:- **R11.1** A stop control halts new model calls and new tool calls when set.\n677:- **R11.2** The agent's own credentials and tools cannot set, clear, delete, or delay the stop control.\n679:- **R11.3** Tool calls already running are cancelled or bounded by a timeout when the stop is set.\n681:- **R11.4** The stop also closes open tool streams, subscriptions, and background tasks.\n683:- **R11.5** Only named operator identities can set the stop control.\n691:- In-flight writes, queued actions, or unattended restarts after the stop → **R12**","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"481b8144-7e21-4ac3-af86-50afc22faa0b","uuid":"b87de0af-3df6-4e51-8de3-63f8d8e0fbcb","timestamp":"2026-10-02T18:01:00.017Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\n  \"brace_checklist\": \"2026-10-01\",\n  \"repo\": \"\",\n  \"commit\": null,\n  \"reviewed_at\": \"2026-10-02T18:00:52Z\",\n  \"scope\": \"TODO: